<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Paris (1815)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1815</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-seventh-coalition">War of the Seventh Coalition</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-paris-1814">Treaty of Paris</a> of November 1815 was signed after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-waterloo">Waterloo</a> and his Hundred Days. It reduced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> to its 1790 borders, imposed an indemnity and an allied army of occupation. A convention signed alongside it placed the Ionian Islands under British protection as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> of the Ionian Islands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-paris-1815.jpg" alt="Treaty of Paris (1815)" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The Great Mule of Eupatoria · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coalition_occupation_of_France_1815.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
